								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=835"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg13252#msg13252"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg13252#msg13252">Re: Relief for us smelly bards.  LOL</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #26 on:</b> December 17, 2004, 04:47:50 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Well, since I started this thread I have a prespective on Melody now since it went live.&nbsp; I spent some time helping guildies grind in Nobles and used melody to debuff chant and mana regen for them outside the group which worked&nbsp; ok&nbsp; but still had lots of missed notes and had to start it again and again.&nbsp; I would never use melody in a 6 man group and only in a raid where I was expected to provide resist and mana regen.&nbsp; I&#039;ve never liked swarming and since I&#039;m 70 and half into the level my points are now 100% for AAs.&nbsp; Melody is questionable as far as I&#039;m concerned but will let time and the younger bards still moving up be the judge.&nbsp; Good luck using this new tool but remember a bard is suppose to adaptable.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13310"></a><a name="new"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=974" title="View the profile of Violo Stratavari">Violo Stratavari</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 7<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=974"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg13310#msg13310"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg13310#msg13310">Re: Relief for us smelly bards.  LOL</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #27 on:</b> December 19, 2004, 12:52:17 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							given a chance to use it, I see some major flaws in the system... First off is the rate of missed notes makes it so you have to keep restarting, there&#039;s no method of compensation.&nbsp; Here I&#039;d say macro&#039;s are still much better.&nbsp; Plus when you miss a note you have to start the melody over again.&nbsp; In case of a missed note on the third song, restarting the melody would mean the 4th wouldn&#039;t get sung at all.&nbsp; Second, there&#039;s no &quot;stop&quot; function.&nbsp; If there is a song withing the 4 song rotatin that you need to use immediately and repeatedly, there&#039;s no real way to stop the melody without alot of jimmying.&nbsp; <br /><br />I think the limited use of melody would be soloing, particularly chant kiting.&nbsp; As to those who would be boxing a bard for AE&#039;s... I still think macro&#039;s are your best bet.<br /><br />Until Melody, catches up with the macro&#039;s that players can build, I still think it&#039;s a noob tool. 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />- Violo Stratavari 67th Bard of Inner Loop
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
<a name="lastPost"></a>
